abstract: >-
  Scurator is an open-source, high-performance, GPU-accelerated bioinformatics framework 
  engineered for automated identification, functional impact scoring, and publication-ready 
  visualization of somatic cancer driver mutations from Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS) 
  Variant Call Format (VCF) datasets. Built in accordance with European Open Science Cloud (EOSC) 
  FAIR principles and Google Open Source Software (OSS) engineering standards, Scurator 
  couples low-level C-extensions (cyvcf2, htslib) with GPU-accelerated vectorized dataframes 
  (RAPIDS cuDF), achieving up to 594x processing speedups over standard CPU tools.

